  "title": "CHAPTER 20: ECONOMIC PLANNING IN INDIA",
  "order": 90,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "r0q0j6a",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "INTRODUCTION TO ECONOMIC PLANNING"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Economic planning in India officially began with the First Five-Year Plan covering the period from 1951 to 1956.",
        "The planned trajectory faced an interruption known as the Plan Holiday from 1966 to 1969.",
        "The Twelfth Five-Year Plan (2012–2017) marked the final Five-Year Plan structure in India.",
        "NITI Aayog replaced the central planning framework starting in 2015 to direct national economic strategy."
      ],
      "id": "1tehdab"
    },
